Z||000023||88formula||11-21-2001||06:30 PM||||If you are building and swapping in a 3.4-liter pushrod motor than you don't want to use the 3.4 injectors or anything bigger. It will just run way too rich! Use the 2.8 injectors and turn up the fuel pressure to around 47 psi at WOT.<P>If you use bigger injectors you are going to have to have the prom chip changed and even then your idle quality will suffer. <P>1, many people actually use the 2.8 injectors with the 3.4 swap not the 3.4 injectors. Ask Ed Parks!<P>2, Stock rating is 14.9 lb. an hour.<P>3, Don't bother getting used injectors because you don't know what you are getting. Most injectors start to clog up after 40k miles.<P>4, there is a noticeable power loss (too rich) when you use larger injectors on a 3.4 unless you have a custom prom made.<P>5, $80 from the Fierostore.   <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||jimmybpei||11-21-2001||07:58 PM||||Travis-- what did you mean when you said . after a little messaging 19# stock mustang units have been the best for MY 2.8 applications. <P>So is there still some work to do after directly installing the ford 19lb injectors.<P>I've got my engine built from bottom to top still trying to research fuel, air and ignition systems for the car, as what combo would post the quickest times (1/4 mile)<P>And what do you need with the palm (program)<BR>and does this allow the palm to tweek you prom (hidden hp)  with the user inputting info??????????<P>Thankx <BR>Jimmy B||||reg||1
Z||000025||terryk||11-21-2001||11:43 PM||||The amount of "hidden" horsepower in normally aspirated GM ECM's is essentually non-existent. Any additional power you can squeeze out will be based on reducing some reliability (lean it out), running more advance (higher octane fuel) or just taking advantage of the production spread (fine tuning for your engine parts).<P>Tweaking to take advantages of engine mods is a different story but the ECM has little affect on the HP. These tweaks just let the engine mods work properly. Most people want custom chips to correct some problem with an expensive modification. The custom chip is needed to allow the mods to work right. <P>Boosted engines are a whole 'nother story.<P>Just like there are no fairies (left) there is no "instant dragster" change in the ECM for NA engines. And not in the 3.4L DOHC either.<P>Of course, I can suck HP out with a few tweakers too......<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||Cooter||11-22-2001||12:08 AM||||Aw, no more fairies! I was hoping the ECM fairy would leave a custom prom under my pillow tonight. Next, you will probably tell me there is no such thing as Santa Claus, the tooth fairy or Michael Jackson.||||reg||1
Z||000027||GTMike||11-22-2001||12:42 AM||||this is good info.  but i'm a little foggy on a few things.<P>keep in mind my questions are for a 3.4 or a 2.8  with a turbo set up.<P>after everything is all hooked up, (pluming and oil lines for the turbo).  the things you have to controle are the timming and the fuel.<BR>am i right so far?<P>for controleing the timming, so there is no detonation  msd boost timming controler.<P>for the fuel i was going to use a riseing rate fule pressure regulator  that should be good up to 7 psi of boost.  <P>now this s-afc  can that be used to completely manage your fuel under boost and off boost?   i would much rather save up some more money and use the s-afc so that i could run closer to 11 psi of boost <P>will the s-afc  be able to add enough fuel to handle say 15  psi of boost with 19# injectors? <P>how does the s-afc work   is it like one of those piggy back computers that you plug inline with your stock ecm?    does it just controle the injector puls? <P>any answers would be great <p>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
